{"files":[{"content":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <utility>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass adjacency_matrix {\n    size_t vertices;\n    vector<unsigned char> data;\n\npublic:\n    explicit adjacency_matrix(size_t n = 0) : vertices(n), data(n * n, 0) {}\n\n    size_t size() const {\n        return vertices;\n    }\n\n    unsigned char *operator[](size_t row) {\n        return data.data() + row * vertices;\n    }\n\n    const unsigned char *operator[](size_t row) const {\n        return data.data() + row * vertices;\n    }\n};\n\nadjacency_matrix readGraph();\n\nbool testIsomorphism(adjacency_matrix &g1, adjacency_matrix &g2);\nbool verifyPermutation(adjacency_matrix &g1, adjacency_matrix &g2, vector<int> &equivalence);\ninline void printPermutation(vector<int> &equivalence);\n\nvector<int> degreeSequence(const adjacency_matrix &graph) {\n    vector<int> degrees(graph.size(), 0);\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < graph.size(); ++i) {\n        const unsigned char *row = graph[i];\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < graph.size(); ++j)\n            degrees[i] += row[j] != 0;\n    }\n    sort(degrees.begin(), degrees.end());\n    return degrees;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    adjacency_matrix g1 = readGraph();\n    adjacency_matrix g2 = readGraph();\n\n    if (!testIsomorphism(g1, g2))\n        cout << \"The graphs are not isomorphic\" << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n\nbool testIsomorphism(adjacency_matrix &g1, adjacency_matrix &g2) {\n    if (g1.size() != g2.size()) return false;\n    if (degreeSequence(g1) != degreeSequence(g2)) return false;\n\n    vector<int> equivalence(g1.size(), 0);\n    vector<int> exchange_counter(g1.size(), 0);\n    int exchange_index = 1;\n    bool isomorphism_found = false;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < equivalence.size(); ++i)\n        equivalence[i] = i;\n\n    if (verifyPermutation(g1, g2, equivalence)) {\n        printPermutation(equivalence);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /*\n     * Permutations are based on Heap's algorithm, which generates all possible\n     * permutations for a given set of elements.\n     */\n    while (exchange_index < g1.size()) {\n        if (exchange_counter[exchange_index] < exchange_index) {\n            if (exchange_index % 2 == 0)\n                swap(equivalence[0], equivalence[exchange_index]);\n            else\n                swap(equivalence[exchange_counter[exchange_index]], equivalence[exchange_index]);\n            if (verifyPermutation(g1, g2, equivalence)) {\n                printPermutation(equivalence);\n                isomorphism_found = true;\n            }\n\n            exchange_counter[exchange_index]++;\n            exchange_index = 1;\n        } else {\n            exchange_counter[exchange_index] = 0;\n            exchange_index++;\n        }\n    }\n    return isomorphism_found;\n}\n\nadjacency_matrix readGraph() {\n    int vertices, edges, source, destination;\n\n    cin >> vertices;\n    adjacency_matrix read(vertices);\n\n    cin >> edges;\n    for (int i = 0; i < edges; i++) {\n        cin >> source >> destination;\n        read[destination][source] = read[source][destination] = 1;\n    }\n\n    return read;\n}\n\nbool verifyPermutation(adjacency_matrix &g1, adjacency_matrix &g2, vector<int> &equivalence) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < equivalence.size(); ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= i; ++j) {\n            if (g1[i][j] != g2[equivalence[i]][equivalence[j]]) return false;\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\ninline void printPermutation(vector<int> &equivalence) {\n    for (auto i : equivalence)\n        cout << i << \" \";\n    cout << endl;\n}\n","path":"src/brute_isomorphism.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A flat row-major byte matrix should reduce allocation and bit-proxy overhead in repeated permutation checks. Comparing sorted row sums first should also reject some non-isomorphic graph pairs before exhaustive search, while retaining the exact search whenever the necessary invariant matches.","notes":"The degree invariant includes diagonal entries, so it remains sound for the source's loop handling. No commands or measurements were run; the controller should assess the added prefilter cost and layout change.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace vector-of-vector<bool> adjacency storage with a contiguous row-major byte matrix, preserving symmetric edge writes and the existing permutation comparison order.","Before permutation enumeration, compare sorted adjacency-row sums, including diagonal entries; reject only when this necessary isomorphism invariant differs, otherwise retain the exact reference-compatible search." ]}